-- 867: Embed the UTAP explainer video in the UTAP claim post.
--
-- Video: youtu.be/dKFqx_F-xnI -- "UTAP AI Tool Claim 2026: Check These 3 Dates Before You Buy"
-- (Tertiary Courses channel). Placed directly after the opening "Short version"
-- paragraph so it sits above the fold, where an explainer earns the most watch
-- time and lifts dwell time on the page.
--
-- Responsive 16:9 wrapper (padding-bottom:56.25%) matching post 452's pattern, so
-- the player scales on mobile instead of overflowing the column. Uses the
-- youtube-nocookie host and loading="lazy" so the embed does not cost anything on
-- first paint or drop tracking cookies before the reader plays it.
--
-- Content rebuilt from the pristine committed migration (866's body) and
-- transformed in-process -- deliberately NOT round-tripped through a DB read,
-- which would decode with errors='replace' and destroy every em-dash. Generation
-- asserted zero U+FFFD, an unchanged em-dash count, and exactly one iframe.
--
-- Idempotent: the UPDATE is guarded on the video id being absent, so a re-run is
-- a no-op. apply.php splits on semicolon-at-EOL, so the UPDATE is ONE line.

UPDATE `mmd_blog_post` SET `content` = '<p><strong>Short version:</strong> if you are a paid-up NTUC member and you complete a UTAP-approved AI course, NTUC will reimburse <strong>50% of what you pay for an approved AI tool subscription</strong> — up to <strong>$250 a year</strong> if you are below 40, or <strong>$500 a year</strong> if you are 40 and above. The support window runs from <strong>1 May 2026 to 30 April 2028</strong>. Below is exactly how to claim it.</p> <div style="position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;margin:24px 0;border-radius:10px;"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/dKFqx_F-xnI" title="UTAP AI Tool Claim 2026: Check These 3 Dates Before You Buy" style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div> <h2>What is the UTAP AI tool subscription claim?</h2> <p>The Union Training Assistance Programme (UTAP) is NTUC''s training benefit for members. It has always covered course fees; from <strong>1 May 2026</strong> it also covers <strong>AI tool subscriptions</strong> — the paid plans professionals actually use day to day, such as ChatGPT Plus, Claude Pro, Microsoft 365 Copilot, Gemini and similar approved tools.</p> <p>The logic behind the scheme is simple: NTUC does not want members to merely <em>attend</em> an AI course and then go back to working the old way. It wants the tool in your hands afterwards. So the subsidy is deliberately sequenced — <strong>learn first, subscribe second, claim third</strong>.</p> <h2>How much can you claim?</h2> <table> <tr><th>Your age</th><th>UTAP support</th><th>Annual cap</th></tr> <tr><td>Below 40</td><td>50% of the subscription fee</td><td>$250 per calendar year</td></tr> <tr><td>40 and above</td><td>50% of the subscription fee</td><td>$500 per calendar year</td></tr> </table> <p><strong>Important:</strong> this cap is <em>shared</em>. The same $250 / $500 annual ceiling covers your UTAP course-fee claims <em>and</em> your AI tool subscription claims combined — it is not a separate top-up. If you have already used your full UTAP allowance on course fees this year, plan your subscription claim for the next calendar year.</p> <h2>Are you eligible? The five conditions</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Paid-up NTUC membership</strong> — before the course starts, throughout the whole course, <em>and</em> at the point you submit the claim. A lapsed month in between is the most common reason claims get rejected.</li> <li><strong>You completed a UTAP-approved AI course</strong> — with at least <strong>75% attendance</strong> and a Certificate of Completion.</li> <li><strong>You subscribed within one year</strong> of completing that course.</li> <li><strong>The subscription start date falls between 1 May 2026 and 30 April 2028</strong> (both dates inclusive).</li> <li><strong>The subscription is for your own use</strong> — you must declare this. Company-paid or fully-sponsored subscriptions do not qualify.</li> </ol> <h2>Step 1: Complete a UTAP-approved AI course</h2> <p>Nothing else in this guide works until this step is done — the claim form literally asks <em>"Attended UTAP Approved AI Course?"</em> and requires your certificate as an upload.</p> <p>Our WSQ AI courses are UTAP-eligible and, for Singaporeans and PRs, already carry <strong>up to 70% SkillsFuture (WSQ) course fee funding</strong> before UTAP is applied. Popular starting points:</p> <ul> <li><a href="{{store direct_url=''wsq-agentic-ai-for-business-process-automation.html''}}"><strong>WSQ - Agentic AI for Business Process Automation</strong></a> — build AI agents that take real work off your plate</li> <li><a href="{{store direct_url=''wsq-agentic-ai-for-social-media-marketing.html''}}"><strong>WSQ - Agentic AI for Social Media Marketing</strong></a> — for marketers who want AI running the content engine</li> <li><a href="{{store direct_url=''wsq-end-to-end-creative-image-generation-with-agentic-ai-and-vibe-coding.html''}}"><strong>WSQ - End-to-End Creative Image Generation with Agentic AI and Vibe Coding</strong></a> — for designers and content creators</li> </ul> <p>Browse the full catalogue of <a href="{{store direct_url=''artificial-intelligence-courses.html''}}"><strong>AI courses in Singapore</strong></a> — over 200 courses across generative AI, agentic AI, AI marketing, data science and AI-assisted coding. Check the course page or ask our team to confirm UTAP approval before you enrol.</p> <h2>Step 2: Subscribe to an approved AI tool</h2> <p>Once you have your certificate, subscribe to an approved AI tool <strong>within one year</strong>. Pick the tool you will genuinely use for work — the whole point of the scheme is adoption, and you will need the payment records at claim time. Keep the tax invoice or receipt, and note the exact <strong>subscription start date</strong>: your six-month claim clock starts from that date, not from your course completion date.</p> <h2>Step 3: Submit your claim on the NTUC U Portal</h2> <p>The claim is made online. Here is the exact click path:</p> <ol> <li>Visit the <strong>NTUC Member Portal</strong> at <a href="https://www.ntuc.org.sg/uportal" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ntuc.org.sg/uportal</a></li> <li>Click <strong>E-Services</strong></li> <li>Log in using your <strong>Singpass</strong></li> <li>Click <strong>Apply Here</strong> under <strong>Union Training Assistance Programme (UTAP)</strong></li> <li>Select <strong>AI Tools Subscription Claim</strong></li> <li>Choose <strong>"Yes"</strong> for <em>"Attended UTAP Approved AI Course?"</em></li> <li>Upload your <strong>Certificate of Completion</strong> for the module, then complete your <strong>AI Course Details</strong> and <strong>AI Tool Subscription Details</strong>, and check that your <strong>bank account details</strong> are accurate for reimbursement</li> <li>Review your application and click <strong>Submit</strong></li> </ol> <h3>Before you hit Submit, have these ready</h3> <ul> <li>Your <strong>Certificate of Completion</strong>, saved and ready to upload</li> <li>Your <strong>AI tool subscription details</strong> — tool name, subscription start date, payment/receipt details</li> <li>Your <strong>bank account information</strong>, correct and current — wrong bank details are the number one cause of delayed reimbursements</li> </ul> <p>Stuck at any point? Call the <strong>NTUC Membership Hotline at 6213 8008</strong>.</p> <h2>The two deadlines that catch people out</h2> <table> <tr><th>Clock</th><th>You have</th><th>Counted from</th></tr> <tr><td>Course &rarr; subscription</td><td>12 months</td><td>Your course completion date</td></tr> <tr><td>Subscription &rarr; claim</td><td>6 months</td><td>Your subscription <em>start</em> date</td></tr> </table> <p>Miss either window and the claim is gone — there is no appeal for a late submission. The safest habit: submit the claim in the same week your subscription is charged, while the receipt is still in your inbox.</p> <h2>Worked example</h2> <p>Priya, 43, is a marketing manager and a paid-up NTUC member. In June 2026 she completes a UTAP-approved WSQ agentic AI course with full attendance. In July 2026 she subscribes to an approved AI assistant at $30/month and commits to a year — $360. She submits her UTAP AI Tools Subscription Claim in August 2026, well inside the six-month window. At 50% support her claim is $180, which sits comfortably under her $500 annual cap (she is 40 and above). Net cost of her tooling for the year: <strong>$180</strong> — and the course fee itself was already WSQ-funded.</p> <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2> <div class="mmd-faq"><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Can I claim if my employer paid for the AI tool?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No. You must declare that the subscription is for your own use. Fully sponsored or company-funded subscriptions are not claimable under this scheme.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Does the AI tool subsidy come on top of my course fee claim?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>No — both draw on the same annual cap of $250 (below 40) or $500 (40 and above). Sequence your claims across calendar years if you want to maximise both.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">What if I took the AI course before 1 May 2026?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>The subscription start date is what must fall within 1 May 2026 to 30 April 2028, and it must be within one year of your course completion. So an earlier course can still qualify, provided the one-year gap and the scheme window both hold.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Do I need 75% attendance?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Yes. UTAP requires at least 75% attendance for the course, and you need the Certificate of Completion to upload with the claim.</p></div></details><details class="mmd-faq-item"><summary class="mmd-faq-q">Which of your courses are UTAP-approved?</summary><div class="mmd-faq-a"><p>Our WSQ AI courses are UTAP-eligible. Check the individual course page or contact our team to confirm approval status for the specific run you are enrolling in — approval is confirmed per course and per intake.</p></div></details></div> <h2>Start here</h2> <p>The subsidy rewards people who actually build AI into their work. The sequence is fixed, so the first move is always the course.</p> <ol> <li>Pick your course from our <a href="{{store direct_url=''artificial-intelligence-courses.html''}}"><strong>AI course catalogue</strong></a> and confirm UTAP approval with our team</li> <li>Complete it with 75%+ attendance and collect your Certificate of Completion</li> <li>Subscribe to your AI tool within 12 months, then claim within 6 months of the subscription start date</li> </ol> <p><a href="{{store direct_url=''artificial-intelligence-courses.html''}}"><strong>Browse AI courses and check your funding eligibility &rarr;</strong></a></p> <p><em>Figures and scheme conditions in this article reflect NTUC UTAP terms published for the 1 May 2026 to 30 April 2028 support period and are provided for general guidance. Always confirm current terms on the NTUC U Portal, as scheme rules can change.</em></p>', `updated_at` = NOW() WHERE `url_key` = 'utap-ai-tool-subscription-claim-guide-singapore' AND `content` NOT LIKE '%dKFqx_F-xnI%';
